    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1183">

                <pb facs="1090" n="832" xml:id="pg832"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/1933</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Collector of Customs at Los Angeles</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Elliott</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1183-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Los Angeles</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>British collier <hi rendition="#italic">Lena</hi>, admittedly a naval tender,
                    arrived to-day San Diego. Master wishes to take on board $1,000 provisions for
                    own crew and $4,000 provisions and large supply of fresh water for vessels
                    salvaging the wrecked Japanese <hi rendition="#italic">Asama</hi> on coast of
                    Mexico. Also wishes to stay additional 24 hours to make repairs to boiler. This
                    office’s opinion excess supplies may not be taken. Wire instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Elliott</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1183-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1183-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated, by telephone, to the Department of State April 6.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
